# File: tests/blender/test_bake_*.py and tests/bdd/features/texture_bake.feature (scenarios map 1:1 to tests)
# Generated from: specs/67-bake-authored-materials-to-contract-compliant-uv-texture-sets/requirements.md
Feature: Bake authored materials to contract-compliant UV texture sets

  @SCN001
  Scenario Outline: Any authored material bakes to the contract texture set
    Given a "Crate" collection of class "standard_prop" with a <kind> material
    When the bake runs
    Then every mesh has exactly one UV map "UVMap"
    And T_Crate_Body_BC, T_Crate_Body_N, and T_Crate_Body_ORM PNGs exist with sRGB, Non-Color, and Non-Color color spaces
    And material "M_Crate_Body" uses only Principled BSDF, Image Texture, Normal Map, Separate Color, and Material Output nodes
    And the pre-bake and baked renders match within the documented tolerance

    Examples:
      | kind          |
      | procedural    |
      | triplanar     |
      | image-texture |

  @SCN002
  Scenario: Tiling environment pieces bake seamless sets and keep their UVs
    Given an "environment_piece" plane whose UVs span 0 to 10 with a UV-periodic material
    When the bake runs
    Then its UV coordinates are unchanged and the map is named "UVMap"
    And each baked texture's opposite edges match within 0.04
    And the texel density check passes

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Desktop and Mobile sets are written at the class resolutions
    Given a "Crate" asset and a budgets override of 256 px Desktop and 128 px Mobile
    When the bake completes
    Then Desktop PNGs are 256 px and Mobile PNGs are 128 px with identical file names
    And the result records texture_bytes_desktop, texture_bytes_mobile, and per-variant texture paths

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Materials over the Mobile limit are merged into one atlas
    Given a "standard_prop" asset with three materials
    When the bake runs
    Then every face uses the single material "M_Crate_Body"
    And one T_Crate_Body BC, N, and ORM set is written

  @SCN005
  Scenario: The operator, a direct call, and the pipeline stage share one implementation
    Given a bakeable "Crate" asset
    When the bake runs through nmggamedev.bake_materials and through bake_asset
    Then both return the same texture paths and summary
    And the pipeline texture stage's sidecar carries the texture paths, byte totals, proof, and summary

  @SCN006
  Scenario: An unrepresentable material fails loudly and restores the asset
    Given a "Crate" material with alpha 0.5
    When the bake runs
    Then it fails with code "texture.bake_failed" naming the material, reason "transparency", and a remediation
    And the original materials and UV maps are restored
    And the pipeline texture stage raises PipelineError "texture.bake_failed" with stage "texture"

  @SCN007
  Scenario: An unchanged baked asset is a cache hit
    Given a "Crate" asset that was already baked
    When the bake runs again unchanged
    Then the result reports cache_hit true
    And no PNG file is rewritten
